  "notes": "**Chat and files, as in D-RATS.**\n\n- **To** is a list: **Everyone (CQCQCQ)** first, then heard stations, then **Other call sign\u2026** to type one.\n- **A tab per station.** Click a station under **Heard**, or receive a message addressed to you, and that station gets its own tab. It shows only the traffic between you and that station, sends only to it, and counts unread messages. \u00d7 closes it.\n- **Clear** (or **Ctrl+L**) empties the current tab. Messages stay in the history and in test recordings; **Show all** brings them back.\n- **Right-click Heard** for **Ping all stations**. Right-click a station for **Open conversation**, **Ping**, **Get version** or **Send file\u2026**. Ping replies show the round-trip time.\n- **Send files from the app:** **Send file\u2026** next to **Send**, or drop a file on the chat. You see the size, station, port and time on air before it goes. When it's done, the station's tab says so.\n- **Received files** go to `Documents\\Aether DV\\Received\\YOUR-CALL`, unless your configuration sets `files_dir`. The chat line has **Show file**, and **Transfers** has **Open received files**.\n- **Cancel** a message that's still queued, or a transfer under **Waiting to send**.\n- **Ctrl+1\u20139** switch tabs.\n\nThe command line still works for everything (`aetherdv-cli send-file \u2026`).\n\nStill **tested on the bench only**: two radios on simplex, no repeaters or D-RATS stations yet.",
